  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Extra Attacks (X)" id="530f-0cee-ee10-d08b" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>A model with a weapon with this rule makes X additional attacks with that weapon's profile in melee. These additional attacks only benefit from special rules listed in that weapon's profile.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gargantuan" id="0e0c-cc60-6353-35e3" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>Uses the official Daemons of the Ruinstorm Gargantuan sub-type. A Gargantuan model ignores special rules that negatively modify its Characteristics (other than Wounds), and counts as ten models when working out whether it is outnumbered. It may only make Reactions triggered by Armiger, Dreadnought, Primarch, Mechanised or Vehicle models, or models with a Wounds Characteristic of 8 or more. Successful Wounds from Poisoned (X) or Fleshbane attacks against it must be re-rolled. It may attack with all of its weapons in each Shooting Attack, including Reactions. No non-Gargantuan model may join its unit, and it may not join a unit without the Gargantuan sub-type. It ignores all effects of Psychic Powers, good or bad, and cannot be Wounded or affected by attacks with Psychic Focus, though Force weapons work against it normally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Instinctive Behaviour (X)" id="0c47-6f24-0e9d-304e" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>At the start of your turn, a unit with this rule that is not within 12" of a friendly Synapse creature takes a Leadership test. If it fails, it follows its instinct until the end of the turn, where X is the type shown on its datasheet: Feed: the unit must move toward the nearest enemy unit and declare a charge against it if able. Hunt: the unit must shoot at the nearest visible enemy unit if able, and may not Advance. Lurk: the unit may not move closer to the enemy, and when it shoots it must target the nearest visible enemy unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Monstrous" id="c2b1-a363-0c2c-c371" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>A living war-beast with Toughness and Wounds instead of Armour Values. A Monstrous model is a model of the Infantry unit type with the official 2.0 Monstrous sub-type: its unit cannot be Pinned; it may fire all of its weapons in each Shooting Attack, including Reactions; it may fire Heavy and Ordnance weapons and count as Stationary even if it moved, and may still declare a charge after shooting; and no model that is not also Monstrous may join its unit. Monstrous models also have Hammer of Wrath (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shadow in the Warp" id="685b-e065-f0bf-7d2e" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>Enemy Psykers within 12" of a model with this rule subtract 1 from their Leadership when making Psychic checks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Synapse Creature" id="b8a2-1f39-60e6-9349" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>Friendly Tyranid units within 12" of one or more models with this rule automatically pass Morale checks and Pinning tests, and ignore Instinctive Behaviour. A Synapse creature itself is never affected by Instinctive Behaviour. Every model with this rule is also treated as a Character.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unnatural Resilience" id="d943-5665-f8ca-caf2" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>The unit is immune to Instant Death. Whenever a model in the unit would suffer Instant Death, it suffers D3 wounds instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hive Mind (X)" id="8118-779a-5fee-b169" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>Every Tyranid psyker knows the Psychic Scream psychic weapon, plus X psychic powers from this discipline, chosen when the army is built. X is shown on its datasheet. The Swarmlord knows every power.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hive Fleet (X)" id="6ef3-1641-fb7e-9d1f" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>When building an army, choose one hive fleet for each detachment. Every unit in that detachment gains Hive Fleet (X), where X is the chosen hive fleet. Unique characters may join any hive fleet, except Old One Eye, who may only join Hive Fleet Behemoth.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Regeneration (X)" id="8cfc-b5df-55c5-05f1" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>A model with regeneration gains Regeneration (X): at the end of each of your turns, if the model has lost any Wounds, roll a D6. On a roll of X or more, it restores one lost Wound, up to its starting value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="3c21-439d-5d53-6927" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="64a9-cd0f-ff50-56e2" hidden="false" publicationId="7478-cf16-4f88-170b">
      <description>Listed on this datasheet but not defined in the conversion doc.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
